@startuml j4-ask-for-a-person
!include c4-sequence.iuml
title J4 Asking for a person
actor "Patient" as Patient <<person>>
box "In the patient's browser"
participant "Patient chat\n(chat.js, sync.js)" as Chat <<container>>
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core <<component>>
database "Browser storage\n(localStorage)" as LS <<store>>
end box
box "Vercel functions"
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix <<container>>
end box
database "Postgres\n(Neon)" as Store <<store>>
box "In the staff browser"
participant "Staff page\n(staff/staff.js,\nstaff/tools.js)" as SP <<container>>
end box
actor "Staff" as Staff <<person>>

== The request ==
Patient -> Chat : taps "Talk to a person",\nor types "Can I speak\nto a human?"
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(message,\nclinic file, language)
Core -> Core : looks in the clinic\nfile first; it has no\nanswer, or only the\ncontact line
note right of Core : A question the file answers\nis answered, not passed on.
Core --> Chat : the person reply,\nstatus "needs human"
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket (question,\nreply, call back)
Core -> LS : the ticket joins\nthis browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : "I am not sure I can\nsettle this myself, so\nI have passed your\nrequest to our team ...";\nbelow it the\ncall-back form
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets\n(the ticket, with\nthis browser's key)
Tix -> Store : a row in the\ntable tickets
== At the desk ==
Staff -> SP : on /staff chooses the\ntype "Asked for a person"
SP --> Staff : the ticket, marked\n"Needs human" and listed\nunder "To call back"
@enduml
